flowchart TD
  %% author: Brad W. Setser | outlet: CFR Follow the Money | date: 2025-09-12
  %% title: The Trump Shock That Wasn't (At Least Not Yet)
  %% url: https://www.cfr.org/articles/trump-shock-wasnt-least-not-yet
  %% topics: US tariffs, trade flows, elasticities, WTO | genre: blog / data analysis

  subgraph L0["Level 0 · Question"]
    Q["`**Question**
      Have Trump's tariffs actually shocked trade flows and the global economy?`"]
  end

  subgraph L1["Level 1 · Priors & assumptions"]
    P1["`**Stated assumption**
      A global tariff works like an exchange rate move: import elasticity of about 0.3 to 0.4, not the bilateral elasticity of about 2`"]
    P2["`**Stated assumption**
      Record tariff revenue means Americans keep importing and paying the tariff`"]
    P3["`**Hidden assumption**
      *Tax- and finance-driven flows (pharmaceuticals, gold) are noise; core trade is the real signal*`"]
  end

  subgraph L2["Level 2 · Evidence"]
    E1["`**Data**
      Annualized trade deficit peaked at $2 trillion in March, fell to $1 trillion, then rebounded to $1.2 trillion in July; imports from Taiwan up over 50 percent year to date; first-term tariffs cut affected trade about 30 percent, and about 50 percent for goods tariffed at 25 percent; high-frequency global trade measures have not slowed`"]
    E2["`**Studies and sources**
      New York Times reporting; U.S. trade data; federal court ruling on tariff authority`"]
  end

  subgraph L3["Level 3 · Mechanisms"]
    M1["`**Front-running**
      Pharmaceutical stockpiling (distorted by tax) and gold flows drive the headline swings`"]
    M2["`**Trade diversion**
      Imports shift from China to Taiwan and Southeast Asia as final assembly relocates`"]
    M3["`**Artificial intelligence investment**
      The data center buildout pushes electronics imports up`"]
    M4["`**Elasticity math**
      A 15 percent tariff times a 0.3 to 0.4 elasticity cuts imports 5 to 6 percent; non-oil imports fall from about 10 to 9.5 percent of GDP`"]
  end

  subgraph L4["Level 4 · Intermediate claims"]
    C1["`**Intermediate claim**
      Excluding pharmaceuticals and gold, U.S. imports are roughly on trend; the shock to trade rules far exceeds the shock to trade flows`"]
  end

  subgraph L5["Level 5 · Conclusion"]
    K["`**Main claim**
      The Trump shock to trade flows has not happened yet, though a modest impact should appear`"]
  end

  subgraph L6["Level 6 · Counterpoints"]
    X["`**Opposing view**
      Reading headline volatility as tariffs crushing trade`"]
    QF["`**Caveat**
      August deals doubled tariffs on Southeast Asia relative to April; fall data may show more impact; the tariffs' legality is unresolved`"]
    R1["`**Other explanation**
      Waiting for tariff relief (autos) replaces front-running; other exporters can take U.S. market share abroad`"]
  end

  P3 --> M1
  E1 --> M1
  E1 --> M2
  E1 --> M3
  P1 --> M4
  E2 --> M1
  M1 --> C1
  M2 --> C1
  M3 --> C1
  P2 --> C1
  M4 --> K
  P3 -->|rule behind it| C1
  C1 --> K
  K -.->|pushes back on| X
  K -. caveat .- QF
  M1 -. other explanation .- R1

  Q ~~~ P1 & P2 & P3
  P1 ~~~ E1
  P3 ~~~ E2

